<title>JAPAN: OSE seeks option trading on 20 stocks - sources.</title>
<headline>OSE seeks option trading on 20 stocks - sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Osaka Stock Exchange (OSE) is seeking to start option transactions on 20 individual shares on July 18, security market sources here said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The OSE is trying to win a consensus from securities houses on the issue, and is set to make a decision at its regular board meeting on April 15, an official at the bourse said.  </p>
<p>The following is the list of the 20 individual stocks the Osaka bourse has suggested to Japan's &quot;Big Four&quot; brokerage houses as likely candidates for the options trading:  </p>
<p>Toray Industries Inc, Nippon Steel Corp, Hitachi Ltd, Toshiba Corp, Mitsubishi Electric Corp, Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd, Sony Corp, Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd, Toyota Motor Co, Nintendo Co Ltd, Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp, Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd, Mitsubishi Corp, Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd, Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd, Sanwa Bank Ltd, Sumitomo Metal Mining Co Ltd, Daiwa Securities Co Ltd, Yamaichi Securities Co Ltd and Nikko Securities Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
